<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela Congress approves Hamaca oil venture.</title>
<headline>Venezuela Congress approves Hamaca oil venture.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's Congress gave its final approval Wednesday to the Hamaca extra-heavy crude venture in a bicamaral session.</p>
<p>The $3.5 billion deal between Atlantic Richfield Co, Texaco Inc, Phillips Petroleum Co and state oil subsidiary Corpoven plans to produce 200,000 barrels per day of extra-heavy Orinoco oil and convert it into lighter crude for export.</p>
<p>Hamaca is one of six such projects designed to exploit Venezuela's estimated 270 billion barrels of extra-heavy Orinoco oil reserves.</p>
<p>((--Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
